  "question": {
    "text": "A current carrying wire heats a metal rod. The wire provides a constant power <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> to the rod. The metal rod is enclosed in an insulated container. It is observed that the temperature <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> in the metal rod changes with time <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> as:<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math><br />where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></math> is a constant with appropriate dimension while <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> is a constant with dimension of temperature. The heat capacity of the metal is:"
  },
